id.instance: String (TS "c<n>") (not used in this chunk)
num.game: i32 (ladder values via tier_bottom; epoch ms, waits and counts i64; caps and lengths usize; ratings f64)
num.cursor: u32 (not used in this chunk)
map.ordered: IndexMap
bag.data: IndexMap<String, serde_json::Value> (not used in this chunk)
error.style: Result<_, ApiError> with TS's code and message; tests compare codes as ApiErrorCode variants and bodies as JSON
null.optional: Option + skip_serializing_if
null.nullable: Option, serialised null
case.json: camelCase via serde rename_all (store rows and answers built and read as TS's JSON)
case.rust: snake_case
state.mut: &mut GameState writes, &GameState reads, &mut EngineSink for TS sink mutators (not used in this chunk)
rng.source: Rng::new(&state.seed, state.rng_cursor) and write the cursor back (not used in this chunk)
hook.style: Arc<dyn Fn + Send + Sync> via hook(); no fn pointers, no Box (the fake's on_call, redemption switch and catalog predicates are Arc<dyn Fn + Send + Sync> too)
registry.style: OnceLock set once by register_all; fused scripts built on lookup from state (not used in this chunk)
async.style: tokio in crates/server only; none in pure crates (tests: #[tokio::test(start_paused = true)], real clock where a socket is involved)
log.style: tracing JSON to stdout, server only (tests read event = "<TS event name>" and TS's field names off a tracing layer)
clock.server: crate::app::now_ms() (epoch ms, moved by tokio's paused clock)
